{"messages": [{"content": "You are Mouth, Lumen’s user-facing response agent. Explain tool results clearly without leaking internal JSON or sentinels.", "role": "system"}, {"content": "Trusted observation:\nIn broadcast television, cord-cutting refers to the pattern of viewers, referred to as cord cutters, cancelling their subscriptions to multichannel subscription television services available over cable, dropping pay television channels or reducing the number of hours of subscription TV viewed in response to competition from rival media available over the Internet such as Amazon Video, Hulu, iTunes, Netflix, Sling TV, and YouTube.\n\nUser request:\nYeah, that's probably even higher today. Any real reason why people want to keep their expensive cable subscriptions these days?", "role": "user"}, {"content": "I can't really say. Do you use providers like Amazon, Hulu, Netflix, or YouTube?", "role": "assistant"}], "metadata": {"agent": "mouth", "manifestCommit": "33c197e4326da227a6119e1c402b4da732ae9b1b", "publicCorpus": {"attribution": "FaithDial by the FaithDial authors and contributors.", "language": "en", "modified": true, "partitionKind": "ml_split", "preferenceContentSHA256": "d5ca14c5d9e7e2c31a364b2aebda7c654c82300311eca9bd590ca59c590d0583", "quality": {"expertAnnotated": false, "humanCorrectedFinal": true, "humanReviewed": true, "piiRegexScreened": true, "rejectedOriginalLabel": "Hallucination", "synthetic": false, "trustedObservationPresent": true}, "selectionScore": {"adapterRelevance": 0.9, "boundaryValue": 0.9, "difficulty": 1.0, "novelty": 0.650039, "overall": 0.897506, "reasons": ["human_reviewed", "quality_profile:human_dialogue_grounding", "role_critical_case", "semantic_boundary_checked"], "sourceConfidence": 1.0, "transformationConfidence": 0.9}, "sourceArtifactSHA256": "51eff8212d804b1954b7eefa8987265750f0412b0b18b534ed2dbe636e524512", "sourceContentSHA256": "7c31dc4f19b3ceaecb970aadddd8226c2962445ff916d5ff8463486c83c4ba8b", "sourceGroupID": "1987fe